    "explanation": "Rider, you get your SGD 4.00 back. Driver, you get SGD 2.00, paid by the platform and never taken from the rider. Neither of you did anything wrong: the app's pin sat at the VivoCity Lobby L ride-hailing pickup and the driver's device placed him at the HarbourFront kerb, 284.95 m away, and neither of you knew.\n\nOn the charge. POL-NS-01 is a conjunctive test and it fails on three limbs. Limb (b): the GPS trace never places the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius - his closest approach across the whole trip was 284.95 m and 0 of his 52 fixes qualified. Limb (c): the effective in-geofence dwell is 0 seconds against the 300 second minimum, a 300 second shortfall. Limb (d): the trip was terminated by the driver with reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE, which is not RIDER_NO_SHOW, RIDER_UNREACHABLE or EXCESSIVE_WAIT - it is the driver's own admission that he could not find the rider. Any single failure makes the fee unchargeable, and three fail.\n\nThe refund then follows from POL-NS-03, which governs exactly this wrong-face-of-the-same-venue case: the driver was stationary for the required dwell at 284.95 m from the pin, outside the 120 m arrival radius but inside the 400 m ceiling. POL-NS-02 yields to POL-NS-03 on these facts, and POL-NS-06 independently produces a full refund of the cancellation-fee line on the dwell shortfall. The fare ledger carries nothing but the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee, so the whole contested amount comes back.\n\nOn the driver's cost. POL-NS-03(ii) applies. The chat log holds only two SYSTEM notifications, so neither party named a sub-location, and the trip record shows 4 registered pickup points for this venue. The mislocation is therefore attributed to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the driver receives a platform-funded goodwill payment of 50 per cent of the fee - SGD 2.00 - charged to the platform and never recovered from the rider. The refund and the goodwill are independent and are never netted.\n\nOn false arrival. POL-NS-05 is not engaged: the 15:12:05 marker was set while the driver was stationary 284.95 m from the pin, under the 300 m threshold and not at or above 15 km/h, and that clause expressly routes such a case to POL-NS-03. No false-arrival referral arises.\n\nOn weight. EV-GPS-00206 is impaired with issue code LOW_SAMPLE_RATE at weight 0.80 (18 s cadence against a nominal 10 s); I name it, and it still carries the position finding because its largest interval is 26 s against the 120 s gap threshold and it holds 52 driver fixes plus the rider track, so it does not meet POL-NS-08 limbs (a) to (d) and is down-weighted under POL-GEN-02 only. Because it carries the deciding position fact, confidence is capped at 0.80, above the 0.70 floor.\n\nOn escalation. POL-NS-09 is not engaged: there is no direct contradiction between admissible artifacts (POL-NS-03 and POL-NS-05 resolve how an arrival marker within 300 m is treated), these two parties have no repeat-dispute history (both counterparty counters read 0), the POL-NS-07 anti-farming check does not trip (1 no-show termination against 187 completed trips in 30 days), and no deciding fact rests solely on an artifact impaired under POL-NS-08. The profile points both advocates raised are credibility context only. The rider's POL-NS-04 exoneration route is not run, because the chat log holds no rider message, but her device track sits within 22.5 m of the pin throughout, confirming she was where the app told her to be. No clause in this case produces a referral."
  },
