    "explanation": "To the rider: your $4.00 cancellation fee is refunded in full. Both sides agree on the facts, and the driver's own GPS trace shows he never entered the VivoCity Lobby L arrival zone — his closest approach to the pin was 284.95 m against the 120 m arrival radius for a large-venue pickup — and the trip was closed with the reason code DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE. POL-NS-01 makes the fee chargeable only if all four of its conditions hold; limb (b) fails on the trace and limb (d) fails on the reason code, and POL-NS-01 itself says a DRIVER_UNABLE_TO_LOCATE trip is decided under POL-NS-03. POL-NS-02's arrival test yields to POL-NS-03 on these facts. This is a wrong-entrance case, not a false-arrival one: the driver was stationary 284.95 m from the pin, under the 300 m false-marker line and not in motion, so POL-NS-05 does not fire and no false-arrival referral arises. Nothing on the fare ledger exists except the $4.00 cancellation line, so the whole contested amount returns to you.\n\nTo the driver: you are not treated as at fault, and you do not walk away with nothing. VivoCity is registered with four pickup points, and the chat log contains only two system notifications — neither of you named a bay, entrance or block. Under POL-NS-03(ii) the mislocation is attributed to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, so the platform pays you a goodwill amount of $2.00, being 50 per cent of the $4.00 fee. That amount is charged to the platform and is never recovered from the rider; the two figures are independent and are not netted. POL-NS-07's 80 per cent compensation is not available, because it operates only where POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full, which it is not; and the anti-farming check does not trip in any event (no_show_terminations_30d is 1, far below the count of 4, and 1/187 is far below the 0.08 rate).\n\nOn confidence and evidence: the GPS trace carries a LOW_SAMPLE_RATE tag at weight 0.8, and both sides disclosed it. Sparse sampling does not disturb a distance measured from coordinates; there is no sampling gap above 120 seconds, the trace holds 52 driver fixes and a full rider track, and the fare line reconciles, so the trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-NS-08 — it is down-weighted under POL-GEN-02 only. The finding survives that discount, and the ruling's confidence is set at the 0.8 carried by the trace that fixes the driver's position. That is above the 0.70 floor, so no escalation is required and no POL-NS-09 trigger is engaged. The rider's own track places her within 22.5 m of the pin throughout, but POL-NS-04 is not engaged: the chat log contains no rider coordination message, only system notifications, and I do not treat that clause as satisfied."
